    "summaryAr": "Pure instant power. Anywhere. We have created the world’s most advanced portable power supplies, bringing freedom to the way our customers work. With you we want to shape a world where advanced technology meets environmental responsibility and create lasting impact. We are working from all over Europe and the US, whether onsite, hybrid or fully remote. Driven by our curiosity and the desire to leave tomorrow’s world ",
    "descriptionAr": "Pure instant power. Anywhere. We have created the world’s most advanced portable power supplies, bringing freedom to the way our customers work. With you we want to shape a world where advanced technology meets environmental responsibility and create lasting impact. We are working from all over Europe and the US, whether onsite, hybrid or fully remote. Driven by our curiosity and the desire to leave tomorrow’s world cleaner than we found it yesterday. Join us in transitioning away from combustion generators to a cleaner alternative for fast, measurable, and real outcomes. What we’ve achieved so far is just the beginning 🚀 As our Customer Success Manager, you make sure our customers get the most out of Instagrid. You train, enable and inspire local decision makers and end users within existing accounts, and you build the brand advocates who grow our business from within. You work closely with our Account Executives and put their account plans into action on the ground. This is a remote role in France, with plenty of time on the road visiting customers. Become part of our success story by... Building relationships: Visit customers regularly and build trusted relationships at local and regional level Executing locally: Put the account plan agreed with the Account Executive into action on the ground Finding new opportunities: Network within accounts to identify new subsidiaries, contacts and untapped potential Making pilots succeed: Guide pilots to success and ensure a strong start for newly sold units through onboarding and training Scaling your impact: Plan and run training days, lunch & learns, trade shows and other events Growing accounts: Engage enough subsidiaries across key accounts to meet expansion targets Being the voice of the customer: Share insights, testimonials and product feedback with the wider team Managing your portfolio: Keep Salesforce accurate and report on portfolio health, product usage and customer satisfaction Experience in customer success, account management or a similar customer-facing role Deep curiosity for our customers’ applications, so you can speak credibly to end users and local decision makers The ability to build trust quickly with end users, local managers and regional decision makers A structured, reliable way of working, with consistent customer contact across a broad portfolio Discipline with data: accurate Salesforce reporting Team spirit: you share field insights proactively and escalate issues early Willingness to travel extensively across France, with a valid driving licence Fluent French and good English What we offer A competitive salary with a fixed and variable component A car allowance 30 days of paid time off Supplementary health insurance (mutuelle) through our partner Death and disability insurance (prévoyance) that also covers your partner and children A monthly home office allowance A fast-growing company with a flat hierarchy The opportunity to join a company at the cutting edge of its field A laptop and a mobile phone At Instagrid, we are deeply committed to equal employment opportunities as we believe in the power of diverse teams. We do not just accept diversity but actively search for the best talent regardless of gender, ethnical origin, age, religion, sexual orientation or place of origin. Working as a team, we treat each other with respect and value each other’s opinions to achieve our common goals. We are looking forward to receiving your application! 🚀 Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow",
