    "summaryAr": "Homa is a global mobile game developer and publisher creating games people love. We partner with studios and internally develop games, having launched over 80 titles, reached over 2 billion downloads, and seen our game All in Hole break into the global top-50 grossing charts. These are milestones, not the finish line. With deep expertise in product and technology, we built Homa Lab, our proprietary platform that give",
    "descriptionAr": "Homa is a global mobile game developer and publisher creating games people love. We partner with studios and internally develop games, having launched over 80 titles, reached over 2 billion downloads, and seen our game All in Hole break into the global top-50 grossing charts. These are milestones, not the finish line. With deep expertise in product and technology, we built Homa Lab, our proprietary platform that gives developers the market intelligence, data tools, and game tech, with AI built-in, to find product–market fit fast and scale mass-market games into lasting experiences players enjoy for years. This is our flywheel: Homa Lab helps studios spot the right ideas early, turn them into games quickly, and reach millions of players. Every launch brings back data and insights that fuel the next hit, making each turn of the loop faster, smarter, and more likely to win. AI supercharges this process, running through everything we do, from everyday tasks to our guiding principles. What powers the loop is talent density. 220+ people from 30+ nationalities, bringing expertise from the world’s best studios and companies. We uphold ambition, curiosity, humility, and focus, and deliver with speed, excellence, and candor. Since the start, we’ve raised $165M from Headline, Northzone, Eurazeo, Bpifrance, and the founders of King, Sorare, and Spotify, people who’ve built and backed the games and platforms we admire, now supporting our drive to create the next ones. At Homa, we are building the next billion-player experiences from the ground up and shaping the future of entertainment. The team You join an 8-person puzzle studio in Istanbul, founded by Peak and Zynga alumni. It's backed by Homa's puzzle, data, art, and UA teams. Its new puzzle game is heading to global launch, and fresh levels are now its biggest growth lever. The opportunity You own the levels players see every week. You work every day with Homa's product director and the studio's level designers, artists, and engineers. You use a level editor and AI tools that generate layouts and estimate difficulty. AI makes you faster, and you stay the brain behind every level. You work remotely from Türkiye. The team is small, and the bar is high. As the studio grows, you can own a family of mechanics or a pack of levels. You can also lead a group of level designers, or move toward a product role. Your responsibilities Build. Your levels keep fresh content reaching players, every single week. Tune. Your difficulty curve makes levels feel hard but fair, so players keep trying. Introduce. New mechanics land smoothly because your levels teach them step by step. Test. You play every level before release, so players only see levels that work. Optimize. You use win rate, attempts and churn data to turn weak live levels into strong ones. Shape. Your ideas on new mechanics and content push the game forward. Accelerate. You use AI to generate layout variants, explore difficulty options and check solvability. What we look for Ownership. You drive outcomes. When something breaks, you fix it instead of explaining why it broke. Proactive. You don't wait for instructions or perfect conditions. You spot what needs doing and do it. Pragmatism. You look for the simplest solution that works, use whatever tools are available, and ship. AI-driven. AI is already part of how you work every day. You've used it to automate, speed up, or rethink. Sharp thinking. You learn fast, reason from facts, and structure your ideas clearly. Motivated. You're ambitious and grounded. You see this opportunity as a chance to learn faster than anywhere else. Requirements Experience. 1+ year in level design, game design or QA on mobile games, ideally puzzle games. Languages. Fluent Turkish and English. You use both every day. Volume with quality. You ship every week and never let quality slip. Tool speed. You work fast in a level editor and pick up new tools quickly. Data sense. You track level data and use it to tune your levels. Puzzle instinct. You play puzzle games a lot and can explain why a level works. AI native. You turn AI into output. You've built tools that generate layouts, check solvability or analyse level data. Bonus points if you have: Shipped levels on a live mobile puzzle game. Experience with Unity or a similar game engine. Even if you don't check every box in our requirements, we encourage you to apply. We value diverse perspectives and backgrounds, and we're more interested in your potential and passion than a perfect match to our checklist. Our process (2 weeks max) Call with our recruiter (30 min). A generalized conversation, and to tell you more about the role. Level design case study. We look at your thinking and your technical skills. Technical interview with the studio's level designers to dive deeper into technicalities. Final interview with the studio founder and Homa's Puzzle lead. Focused on motivation, values, and fit. Benefits Why Homa Exceptional growth. We hire people of outstanding potential, then put them where they can grow fastest. Your scope and your rewards grow with what you deliver, not with tenure. Real ownership. No layers between you and the result. You own outcomes, not tasks, whatever your level. Direct impact. Your work moves the business and shapes where Homa goes next. Decisions are made fast, and you see the results in the numbers. AI at the core. With access to the best AI tools, you'll help shape how an AI-first company works, and your time goes where your judgment matters most. High talent bar. Our teams are small, with people from the best companies, and the talent around you will push you to grow. What we offer Building great games starts with building a great place to work. Here's what you can expect: Comprehensive benefits. Depending on where you're based, you'll get perks such as health insurance, meal vouchers, public transport, gym membership, and more. A brand-new Paris HQ. A desk in our new office in the heart of Paris, w",
