    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. An overview of this role As a Senior Recruiter, Public Sector GTM, you'll build the go-to-market (GTM) teams that drive GitLab's growth across U.S. federal, state, local, and education customers. In this senior individual contributor role, you'll partner with Public Sector leaders across Sales, Solutions Architecture, Customer Success, Professional Services, Field Operations, and Enablement, owning searches from intake through close. You'll build inclusive pipelines, use data and market insight to guide hiring decisions, and act as a trusted talent advisor to Public Sector leadership. What you’ll do Manage full-cycle searches for Public Sector Account Executives, Solutions Architects, Customer Success, Professional Services, and Sales Operations roles. Deliver against agreed recruiting goals and key metrics, with accurate, timely documentation in Greenhouse. Lead intake conversations to align hiring teams on role scope, segment, territory, quota and ramp expectations, citizenship and clearance requirements, interview plans, and timelines. Support Federal Civilian, Department of Defense, Intelligence Community, and State, Local, and Education searches. Build research-based, diversity-focused sourcing strategies for a constrained talent market. Balance applicants, passive talent, referrals, internal talent, veteran and military-transition talent, and targeted outreach, including candidates with active or previously held security clearances and experience with government agencies, systems integrators, and contract vehicles. Partner with Public Sector leaders on structured, equitable interviews with clear competencies and actionable feedback. Challenge assumptions and escalate risks or blockers early. Use talent-market research, compensation and on-target earnings (OTE) benchmarks, funnel metrics, and candidate feedback to shape search strategy. Plan hiring around public sector buying cycles, including the federal fiscal year-end. Assess sales candidates on track record, quota attainment, deal complexity, and experience with long, procurement-driven sales cycles relevant to GitLab's Public Sector segments and approach. Deliver a thoughtful candidate experience through disciplined pipeline management, proactive communication, timely feedback, and offer negotiations that clearly explain compensation and OTE. Coach less experienced recruiters and improve recruiting practices by sharing reusable resources, using artificial intelligence (AI) responsibly, and representing GitLab's mission, values, and culture. What you’ll bring Senior-level recruiting experience, with a track record of independently owning full-cycle searches and handling complex, hard-to-fill roles. Public Sector, federal, or government-focused sales recruiting experience, or deep familiarity with government sales segments, quotas, OTE, ramp time, territory design, and procurement-driven sales cycles. Working knowledge of how citizenship, clearance, and background investigation requirements affect sourcing, interview timing, and offer-to-start timelines. Experience building stakeholder trust, influencing without authority, and managing hiring team expectations at the manager level and above. Experience building proactive, diversity-focused sourcing strategies and balanced pipelines in niche or credential-restricted talent markets, using funnel insights to guide practical actions. Strong organization across multiple requisitions and clear written and verbal communication across time zones, with attention to detail and candidate care. Experience with an applicant tracking system and recruiting tools such as Greenhouse, Metaview, LinkedIn Recruiter, LinkedIn Insights, SeekOut, ClearanceJobs, or comparable platforms. Ability to evaluate AI-generated work, protect confidential information, and share responsible workflows with team members. Technology or business-to-business (B2B) software recruiting experience is helpful, not required. About the team You'll join a globally distributed, remote-first Talent Acquisition team where clear communication and reliable follow-through matter. Guided by GitLab's operating principles, including Speed with Quality, Ownership Mindset, and Customer Outcomes, we take ownership, move with urgency and rigor, and focus on hiring outcomes that matter to our internal customers. We share learnings and create reusable resources to continually improve the quality and consistency of hiring across GTM teams. The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role's base salary r",
