    "summaryAr": "About the team OpenAI’s Industrial Compute team builds the data center infrastructure that supports our research and products. Procurement and Sourcing partners with Engineering, Construction, Deployment, Finance, and suppliers to secure the critical equipment needed to bring new compute capacity online. About the role We’re hiring an Owner-Furnished Equipment (OFE) Demand Planner for OpenAI’s self-build data center ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the team OpenAI’s Industrial Compute team builds the data center infrastructure that supports our research and products. Procurement and Sourcing partners with Engineering, Construction, Deployment, Finance, and suppliers to secure the critical equipment needed to bring new compute capacity online. About the role We’re hiring an Owner-Furnished Equipment (OFE) Demand Planner for OpenAI’s self-build data center portfolio. Long-lead equipment decisions often come before site schedules, designs, and funding are final. This role helps OpenAI make those decisions early enough to keep deployments on schedule. Key Responsibilities Own and publish the OFE demand baseline for self-build data centers. Translate the capacity roadmap and reference designs into equipment quantities and delivery windows by site, building, and phase. Work backward from equipment need-by dates to set deadlines for design decisions, funding approvals, capacity reservations, and purchase orders. Assess supply coverage with Supply Planning using supplier capacity and lead times validated by Sourcing and production and delivery commitments from Manufacturing Operations. Lead planning reviews with Engineering, Construction, Deployment, and Finance to resolve changes in scope, quantities, and delivery dates. Escalate decisions that put deployment milestones at risk. Model the schedule impact of supply shortages and recommend where to shift deliveries, reallocate equipment, or reserve additional capacity. Provide the OFE demand baseline and forecast changes to the broader Compute Supply & Demand Plan. Qualifications Experience owning a demand, supply, materials, or integrated business planning process for complex hardware or capital equipment. Sound judgment when inputs are incomplete or changing, with the ability to explain assumptions and uncertainty clearly. Experience using supplier lead-time and purchasing data in a project-based planning environment. Strong analytical skills and the ability to explain trade-offs clearly to technical and executive audiences. Experience influencing decisions across teams and with external partners without direct authority. Preferred Skills Experience with data centers, critical facilities, industrial construction, or another capital-intensive, multi-site environment. Familiarity with owner-furnished equipment or long-lead electrical and mechanical infrastructure. Experience improving forecast accuracy, supply coverage reporting, or planning processes using ERP, planning, or analytics tools. Internal review notes Confirm the formal title and level, work location and travel expectations, headcount, and compensation before posting. The plan is for the OFE demand planning backfill to move from Kartik Reddy to Pam Whalen; confirm the position transfer before opening the requisition. Confirm the forecast publishing cadence and escalation path for unresolved procurement decisions. Confirm the equipment categories in scope. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
