    "summaryAr": "Lightly AG is a Zurich-based AI company and ETH/HSG spin-off, backed by Y Combinator and top-tier investors. Our machine learning and computer vision technology is trusted by global leaders in autonomous driving, medical imaging, and visual inspection. We’re looking for reliable, technically minded freelancers to support an AI operations project involving the monitoring of autonomous digital workflows. You'll oversee",
    "descriptionAr": "Lightly AG is a Zurich-based AI company and ETH/HSG spin-off, backed by Y Combinator and top-tier investors. Our machine learning and computer vision technology is trusted by global leaders in autonomous driving, medical imaging, and visual inspection. We’re looking for reliable, technically minded freelancers to support an AI operations project involving the monitoring of autonomous digital workflows. You'll oversee day-to-day activity, respond to alerts, troubleshoot issues, and intervene when human oversight or approval is required. This is a remote, four-week freelance contractor opportunity with scheduled shifts across time zones, including nights and weekends. Tasks What you'll be doing Monitor autonomous digital workflows and operational activity through a web-based interface, identifying errors, unusual behavior, and situations requiring human intervention Remain available and responsive throughout scheduled shifts , acknowledging urgent alerts in Slack within 10 minutes Handle routine operational requests and troubleshoot issues using established procedures and escalation guidelines Review and approve or deny certain actions within predefined limits , escalating sensitive decisions, financial commitments, or exceptions to authorized team members Investigate incidents by reviewing activity logs, error messages, and system outputs to reconstruct what happened, identify likely causes, and flag anything that cannot be verified Intervene in critical situations , including pausing workflows or escalating potential risks when necessary and permitted by the project guidelines Document incidents, operational issues, and human interventions , maintaining clear records of actions taken, outcomes, and unresolved concerns Provide concise shift handovers , summarizing outstanding issues, important developments, and recommended next steps for the incoming team The project focuses on monitoring advanced AI systems performing real-world digital operations. Your role is to ensure that activity remains within established guidelines, identify and resolve operational issues, and provide reliable human oversight when automated systems encounter limitations or require approval. Requirements You're a strong candidate if you: Have fluent written and spoken English , with the ability to communicate clearly and concisely during operational incidents Have experience in technical support, quality assurance (QA), digital operations, IT support, or a similar role involving troubleshooting and monitoring digital workflows Are comfortable using Google Sheets, Excel, Slack, and web-based operational tools to track activity, communicate updates, and document issues Can interpret technical logs, error messages, and structured data , including basic JSON, to investigate problems and identify relevant information Have hands-on experience with AI tools such as Claude or Codex , and a basic understanding of how AI systems work and where they may fail Have strong problem-solving skills and sound operational judgment , particularly when deciding whether to intervene, follow established procedures, or escalate an issue Are highly reliable and responsive , with the ability to remain attentive and available throughout agreed shifts, including nights or weekends where applicable Have excellent attention to detail and can accurately document incidents, actions, and outstanding issues Can work independently under time pressure while consistently following operational guidelines and escalation procedures Preferred qualifications: Previous experience monitoring automated systems, AI agents, or other complex digital workflows Experience with incident management, operational escalation, or technical troubleshooting Familiarity with APIs, automation tools, or basic scripting Experience working in shift-based operations or providing support across multiple time zones Benefits Fully remote — work from anywhere Hourly freelance contract with scheduled shifts Opportunity to work on a cutting-edge AI operations project involving autonomous systems Gain practical experience monitoring advanced AI workflows and supporting real-world AI deployments Send us your CV along with your time zone, availability (including any nights or weekends you can cover), and a brief example of a technical or operational issue you've investigated and resolved. If applicable, we'd also love to know about your experience with AI tools, technical support, incident management, or monitoring automated systems. We look forward to hearing from you! Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow",
