    "summaryAr": "About the Team Technology Sourcing is part of OpenAI’s Finance team. We partner with Product, Engineering, and the Partnerships Team early in development, when the choice of a technology or data provider can shape what teams build and how quickly they can ship. On this team, you’ll help bring new products to market faster, turn supplier partnerships into new sources of revenue and build scalable commercial models. Yo",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team Technology Sourcing is part of OpenAI’s Finance team. We partner with Product, Engineering, and the Partnerships Team early in development, when the choice of a technology or data provider can shape what teams build and how quickly they can ship. On this team, you’ll help bring new products to market faster, turn supplier partnerships into new sources of revenue and build scalable commercial models. Your work ultimately supports OpenAI’s mission to ensure that artificial general intelligence benefits all of humanity. About the Role As Senior Manager, Technology Sourcing, you’ll lead supplier deals that help OpenAI launch new products in both consumer and enterprise spaces. You’ll take deals from requirements and evaluate vendors through negotiation, approval, and launch. You’ll get involved while teams are still making product decisions, when the choice of partner can change what ships and how quickly. You will directly support Product and Engineering teams who work on cutting edge products such as Codex, Sites and Dots and be at the forefront of product development for consumer and enterprise customers. You will also work with cross-functional partners including legal, security and privacy to get relevant deal approvals. In this role, you will: Run high-velocity deals end-to-end: from vendor strategy and RFPs through negotiation, legal and security reviews, contracting, and go-live. Coordinate supplier onboarding, collect required documents and track dependencies through completion. Drive approval follow-through with Legal, Security, Privacy, Finance and other reviewers. Partner with Product and Engineering to ensure external vendors can support new product launches without blocking delivery or increasing risk. Structure contracts and pricing models that preserve optionality, support rapid scaling, and minimize long-term lock-in and switching costs. Maintain accurate deal records, status updates, decisions and next actions. Support sourcing requests, renewals, evaluations and change orders. Act as the control plane between fast-moving product teams and external dependencies, ensuring speed without sacrificing governance, compliance, or economics. You might thrive in this role if you: 8+ year experience in technology sourcing, or commercial negotiations in a high-growth, product-driven environment with a strong focus on software. Strong cross-functional leadership—able to align Product, Engineering, Legal, Security, and Finance around complex, high-stakes decisions. Comfort operating in regulated or high-risk domains (payments, identity, data, financial or health-adjacent infrastructure). A track record of negotiating commercial, technical, and data-driven agreements with software technology vendors. The ability to move fast in ambiguity while maintaining commercial discipline, compliance, and risk awareness. Strong analytical skills to evaluate pricing models, volume ramps and vendor risk in the context of revenue and product growth. An ownership mindset—you independently drive deals, resolve blockers, and close outcomes that materially impact product launches and revenue. A desire to accelerate OpenAI’s mission by enabling better vendor partnerships, faster launches, and more effective execution at scale. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
