    "summaryAr": "About the Team We are a small, fast-moving team that builds and scales OpenAI’s B2B partnerships. Our work spans independent software vendors (ISVs), Marketplace, and emerging partner initiatives. We build the programs, infrastructure, and operating models that help partners launch successfully, generate sustained usage and revenue, and grow alongside OpenAI. About the Role In this role, you will build the operating ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team We are a small, fast-moving team that builds and scales OpenAI’s B2B partnerships. Our work spans independent software vendors (ISVs), Marketplace, and emerging partner initiatives. We build the programs, infrastructure, and operating models that help partners launch successfully, generate sustained usage and revenue, and grow alongside OpenAI. About the Role In this role, you will build the operating foundation the team needs to scale, including processes, data infrastructure, analytics, and partner incentives. You will define how we measure the health of our ecosystem and the performance of individual partners, then use those insights to recommend where we invest and which partner behaviors we incentivize. This is a hands-on, zero-to-one role. The tools, data, and processes you need will not always exist yet. You will work directly with Partnerships to determine what matters, build the first version, and improve it as the team learns. You know when a spreadsheet is enough and when it is time to build something more durable. Success means partners launch faster, more partners generate sustained usage and revenue, and the team can scale without a proportional increase in manual work. In this role, you will: Establish the operating model for Marketplace and related B2B partner programs, including deal review, partner onboarding, solution reviews, launches, ownership, and escalation paths. Build the data infrastructure, reporting, and operating rhythms used to measure partner activation, pipeline, adoption, usage, revenue, and overall ecosystem health. Connect and validate data across existing systems, create dashboards and business reviews, investigate what is driving performance, and recommend where the team should invest. Shape partner incentives and benefits using partner feedback, performance data, and program economics. Define eligibility, identify the behaviors we want to encourage, and work with Partnerships and Finance to test and scale what works. Turn priorities into execution plans with clear owners, milestones, dependencies, and decisions. Work across Partnerships, Product, Engineering, Data Science, Sales, Finance, Legal, and Accounting to resolve blockers and carry initiatives from planning through launch and ongoing operation. Build repeatable workflows and automation that reduce manual work while improving the partner experience. You might thrive in this role if you: Have 5–7 years of experience in strategy and operations, business operations, strategic finance, partner programs, or a related role. Have built reporting, dashboards, incentive programs, and scalable operating workflows from scratch—and successfully driven their adoption. Are comfortable working directly with data and have hands-on fluency with spreadsheets, SQL, BI tools, and CRM data. Have led complex, cross-functional initiatives from planning through delivery, including work with Finance, Legal, and Accounting. Bring strong business judgment and analytical curiosity, and can move comfortably between detailed execution and broader strategic questions. Take ownership of ambiguous problems, build practical first versions, and improve them quickly based on what you learn. Communicate clearly, build trust across functions, and create momentum without relying on formal authority. Have experience with B2B software, ISVs, marketplaces, or partner ecosystems. This is helpful but not required. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
