    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. As a Staff Technical Writer at GitLab, you’ll shape how users, and the AI agents working on their behalf, understand, adopt, and succeed with GitLab. You’ll partner with engineers, product managers, designers, and UX researchers to turn features and design decisions into clear, scalable documentation and intuitive UI text across multiple product stages and sections. As AI increasingly drafts and reviews our content, you’ll bring the judgement that upholds quality and the system thinking that scales that judgement across our documentation. When you see the same problem repeating, you’ll fix the cause rather than just the page, whether that’s through a style guide update, a lint rule, or an AI skill. You’ll model effective use of AI, lead improvements to our docs site and processes, and contribute to one of the world’s largest open-source projects while engaging with our wider community.&nbsp; What you’ll do Own and maintain documentation across product areas (which GitLab organizes by engineering stages and sections), driving improvements and balancing priorities. Champion AI best practices by modeling approved tool use, establishing governance and quality checks, and integrating AI workflows that improve efficiency and quality. Lead efforts to improve the product user experience through UI text, creating model examples and improving the style guide. Design scalable information architecture and content types optimized for both human readability and AI retrieval. Model review practices that improve the quality of contributions and feed back into AI review flows. Design and lead process improvements. Identify systemic problems and the most efficient solution, building alignment with stakeholders and driving adoption. Partner with engineers to translate documentation, content-quality, and user needs into improvements to documentation systems and docs-site functionality. Use data to prioritize work, measure impact, and establish team KPIs. Lead large cross-stage content initiatives, driving collaboration across functions to achieve shared customer and company outcomes. Address feedback from internal teams, customers, support, and community contributors, identifying patterns for wider improvements. Act as a thought partner to management on technical and project decisions, and act as primary lead for a specialist domain such as AI, UX writing, metrics, or tooling. Mentor technical writers and team members on best practices and prioritization. What you’ll bring End-to-end expertise in planning, researching, writing, and editing software documentation. UX and content design skills, with a track record of refining interface text, labels, and naming conventions to improve the product user experience. Experience designing and using AI workflows, including evaluating and refining AI-generated output and guiding quality checks for others. Proficiency working in a docs-as-code environment, using the same workflows and tooling as engineering, operations, and product teams. Fluency using the Linux shell and command-line Git, coupled with general familiarity with one or more programming languages. Excellent grammar, minimalist documentation design skills, and effective information architecture. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to triage and prioritize numerous issues and projects across stages and sections. A track record of leading cross-team projects and process improvements, building alignment with stakeholders, and driving adoption. Data-driven decision making, using analytics and feedback to guide content strategy and demonstrate impact. The ability to succeed in a remote, globally distributed environment, including collaborating across countries and time zones, and to model respectful, professional communication. Adaptability and readiness to work in a rapidly changing environment. Familiarity with DevSecOps tools and open-source software is helpful, not required. About the team Our technical writing team works at the intersection of product, engineering, design, and marketing. We define how GitLab’s features are communicated across documentation and UI text, and we influence product direction by bringing a deep understanding of how words shape user success in a rapidly evolving DevSecOps platform. We also manage the systems that ensure quality at scale, from the governance and orchestration of AI workflows to deterministic testing and linting. Guided by GitLab’s operating principles, we work in a globally distributed, remote-first environment where clear communication and reliable follow-through matter. The base salary range for this role’s listed ",
