    "summaryAr": "Global Transportation Program Manager About the role Develop, improve, and scale employee transportation programs and communications across Bay Area and global offices. Translate priorities into practical, data-informed programs, consistent employee experiences, and repeatable launch resources, while coordinating local stakeholders and vendors. This position is based in San Francisco, with the requirement of being in",
    "descriptionAr": "Global Transportation Program Manager About the role Develop, improve, and scale employee transportation programs and communications across Bay Area and global offices. Translate priorities into practical, data-informed programs, consistent employee experiences, and repeatable launch resources, while coordinating local stakeholders and vendors. This position is based in San Francisco, with the requirement of being in the office 3 days per week . In this role, you will Lead employee-facing transportation programs, TDM initiatives, commuter benefits coordination, and multimodal commute engagement across offices. Own transportation communications, employee resources, enrollment journeys, feedback channels, and change-management plans in partnership with Internal Communications and local Workplace teams. Analyze commute demand, headcount trends, home-location density data where appropriately available, utilization, and employee feedback to propose program improvements. Assist Global Transportation Programs, Senior Manager, in global expansion priorities and standardizations. Coordinate transportation assessments and implementation plans for new or expanding offices, working with Real Estate, Workplace Operations, Benefits, Payroll, Legal, and vendors. Build dashboards and concise business cases that assess adoption, accessibility, employee experience, cost effectiveness, and service options. Manage assigned program vendors or contractors and oversee implementation of approved strategic initiatives; partner with Operations on service changes. What we are looking for Experienced transportation, TDM, mobility, or workplace program manager with strong program development, employee communications, analytical judgment, stakeholder management, and hands-on execution skills. Global or multi-site experience is a plus. You might thrive in this role if you: Have 7+ years of experience delivering effective commuter programs and TDM strategies at a major company Have a background in city planning, transportation planning, and/or project management and experience collaborating and making decisions alongside cross functional teams. Masters in transportation planning a plus Experience managing communications to a diverse group of users and navigating various levels of feedback Excel at at building and leveraging relationships with external vendors, consultants, and internal teams, and can drive accountability Bring a collaborative and proactive approach to project management and delivery Reporting line: Global Transportation Programs, Senior Manager. San Francisco based. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
