    "summaryAr": "About the team Customer Education helps enterprises develop the capabilities their workforce needs to use AI effectively, build and deploy AI solutions, and get more value from OpenAI’s products. About the role We’re looking for a hands-on technical educator who enjoys building with AI and helping others learn to do the same. You’ll create practical education for enterprise developers building with OpenAI’s APIs and ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the team Customer Education helps enterprises develop the capabilities their workforce needs to use AI effectively, build and deploy AI solutions, and get more value from OpenAI’s products. About the role We’re looking for a hands-on technical educator who enjoys building with AI and helping others learn to do the same. You’ll create practical education for enterprise developers building with OpenAI’s APIs and working with Codex. You’ll turn real customer use cases into clear lessons, working examples and hands-on labs, building on our established portfolio of bootcamps, webinars and technical content. The goal is to help builders develop skills they can apply to their own applications and development workflows. This role combines technical development, learning design and live teaching. You’ll build and test what you teach, work directly with learners and create resources that can be reused across in-person, live virtual and self-paced learning. Working closely with the Builder Education team, you’ll independently own defined content, lab and delivery workstreams. You’ll partner with technical experts and customer-facing teams to keep learning accurate, useful and current as products evolve. In this role, you will: Build practical technical education. Turn customer needs into clear learning objectives, lessons, demonstrations and exercises. Sequence concepts, practice, feedback and assessments so learners can build and apply new skills. Create hands-on labs and learning environments. Build working examples and reliable, secure lab infrastructure. Use automation and platform integrations to make setup, access and delivery repeatable as programs grow. Teach directly and improve through practice. Deliver in-person bootcamps and live virtual sessions, explain technical concepts clearly and help learners troubleshoot. Use their questions and feedback to improve the experience. Own content from concept through launch. Work with technical experts to develop, test and publish content, code examples and labs. Maintain technical accuracy and update materials as products and customer needs change. Make learning reusable. Adapt content across bootcamps, webinars and self-paced courses, and create resources that customers, internal teams and partners can use independently. Run defined program workstreams. Manage scope, timelines and dependencies, coordinate contributors and support program operations. Build repeatable processes that keep content, environments and delivery ready for learners. Use evidence to improve learning. Assess whether builders can apply what they learn, and work with program and analytics partners to understand how programs support product adoption and continued use. You might thrive in this role if you: Have hands-on technical experience in software development, cloud infrastructure or AI workflows, and have built applications, integrated APIs, used Git or other version control and worked with coding agents. You can share examples of applications, API integrations or AI workflows you personally delivered. Can turn complex technical topics into clear learning experiences, with purposeful practice and ways to assess whether learners can apply new skills. Have built and maintained hands-on labs or technical learning environments for external customer or developer audiences, with attention to reliability, security and ease of use. Are an engaging teacher and clear writer who can explain technical decisions, respond to learner questions and troubleshoot live. Stay curious about AI, explore new capabilities firsthand and test the code and workflows you teach. You use learner feedback to improve your work. Have independently owned a technical learning program from an ambiguous brief through launch and iteration, making practical scope decisions and contributing across content, teaching and program operations. Have experience beyond education-only settings, working with product, engineering or customer teams. Experience in a fast-paced tech environment is preferred. Nice to have: Experience with infrastructure automation tools such as Terraform and integrations that support technical labs. Experience with learning platforms, LMS/SCORM, certification or assessment design, or learning analytics. Relevant technical certifications or experience delivering technical training across live and self-paced formats. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage;",
