    "summaryAr": "In 2026, we launched Computer, the defining product for the new era of agentic AI. Millions of people and teams adopt Perplexity and Computer on their own, and our enterprise marketing programs bring in thousands more leads. We've grown this far without a marketing automation platform or a dedicated Pipeline Operations team. We're ready to build both. We're hiring our first Head of Pipeline Operations. You'll choose ",
    "descriptionAr": "In 2026, we launched Computer, the defining product for the new era of agentic AI. Millions of people and teams adopt Perplexity and Computer on their own, and our enterprise marketing programs bring in thousands more leads. We've grown this far without a marketing automation platform or a dedicated Pipeline Operations team. We're ready to build both. We're hiring our first Head of Pipeline Operations. You'll choose and implement our first marketing automation platform, own how every marketing and product lead is enriched and routed, and work with Data Science and Growth on how MQLs and PQLs are scored and qualified. You'll own the systems our BDR team prospects in and co-own execution support with BDR leadership. And you'll build the campaign operations, attribution and reporting that connect B2B and enterprise marketing to pipeline and revenue. You'll report to the Head of Revenue Operations and build a team. Your first direct report is a GTM Engineer, who owns our enrichment platform, lead routing and warehouse-to-Salesforce syncs. You set the definitions and priorities, and the GTM Engineer is your force multiplier for delivering them. Tech stack: Salesforce | Snowflake | Clay | Marketing automation (you'll choose it) | Reverse ETL (Hightouch or similar) | Routing and scheduling (Default, Chili Piper or similar) | Computer Why Perplexity is different Craftsmanship. We build high quality, tasteful products targeting both the AI native and AI curious. Ownership. You identify the problem, design the solution and ship it. Entrepreneurship. We think like founders, act with urgency, and hustle to deliver for each other and our users. Scholarship. Work among highly talented peers, pursuing knowledge and truth, upleveling ourselves, our teams, and our products. Partnership. We amplify each others' strengths, break down silos, and give selflessly to help our colleagues deliver excellence. What you'll do Build and lead the Pipeline Operations team. Manage the GTM Engineer from day one, set the roadmap, and hire as the function grows. Stay hands-on while the team is small. Select and implement our marketing automation platform. Run the evaluation, then lead the rollout: data model, lifecycle stages, templates, permissions and migration of existing B2B email programs. Own the lead lifecycle. Define lifecycle stages, qualification criteria, handoff SLAs and recycle rules with Marketing and Sales leadership, and enforce them consistently across our systems. Own enrichment and routing, and make scoring drive action. You are accountable for every lead being complete and sent to nurture or to a BDR, AE or Account Manager within SLA, and you direct the GTM Engineer who runs these systems. Data Science owns our scoring models, including product-qualified lead scoring. On marketing-qualified lead scoring, you represent Marketing and Sales: define what qualifies, supply engagement signals and agree handoff thresholds. Run product-qualified leads in parallel with marketing-qualified leads. PQLs flow to BDRs too. Work with Growth, who publish the product usage signals behind them, and Data Science, who score them, on how PQLs are qualified, routed and followed up, with the same lifecycle, SLAs and reporting as MQLs. Own BDR systems, and co-own execution support with BDR leadership. You own the infrastructure: the sequencing, dialing and research tools, the Salesforce lead and account queues, and the integrations between them. Lead the implementation and evolution of this toolset, a combination of internally built applications and vendor solutions, with the GTM Engineer and our GTM Platform team delivering the builds. BDR leadership takes the primary role in daily and weekly use: building sequences and plays, activating target lists, actioning signals and monitoring SLAs on routed leads. They own the substance inside the systems and the business results across their team. You own resolving system and data issues, and reporting activity by rep and by play. Stand up account-based marketing and sales as a motion. With Sales and Marketing leadership, select and tier target accounts by fit, intent and product usage, using the account fit scores Data Science publishes, and set the investment for each tier. Map buying groups and work with Data Science on an account-level engagement score that tells BDRs and AEs when to act. Design coordinated plays across email, ads, events and outbound, with clear triggers, owners and SLAs. Measure by account: coverage, engagement, meetings, pipeline and win rate against non-target accounts. Own nurture and campaign infrastructure for B2B and enterprise marketing, and co-own execution with Marketing. You own the build: nurture enrollment rules, segments, templates, tracking, QA, a repeatable launch process and a clean Salesforce campaign structure. Marketing takes the primary role in what runs through it: strategy, audiences, offers, content, calendar and budget. They own the substance of the programs and the pipeline they produce. You own launching on schedule and reporting performance by program. Own attribution and marketing reporting. Build the tracking and lead source model, define how we measure marketing-sourced and marketing-influenced pipeline, and own the dashboards and weekly funnel review. Marketing and Revenue Operations should report the same numbers. Protect consent and deliverability. Own consent, suppression and sending-domain health for B2B and enterprise marketing email, and agree shared rules on contact frequency and sending domains with Growth, who own product and consumer lifecycle messaging. Partner with Growth on web conversion. Growth owns the website and sign-up flows. You own what happens to a B2B lead after capture: form fields, tracking, consent and a clean handoff into our systems. Own the marketing technology stack, its budget and the team's operating rhythm. Evaluate vendors and manage renewals. Run intake and prioritization, document every system,",
